10. Key Takeaways

- Reverse-proxy headers can influence backend application behaviour.
- Trusting user-controlled host information can compromise password-reset URL generation.
- A cryptographically strong token can still be exposed through insecure URL construction.
- Reset tokens and session cookies have different purposes.
- HTTP status codes must be interpreted alongside application behaviour and supporting evidence.
- Mobile tools can support practical web-security investigations, although they do not replace every desktop testing capability.

